{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/2.5D Depth Cards and Parallax.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/2.5D Depth Cards and Parallax.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"2.5 d depth cards and parallax 2.5 d depth cards and parallax","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/2.5D Depth Cards and Parallax.md","fileName":"2.5D Depth Cards and Parallax.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"2.5D Depth Cards and Parallax","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:17\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Matte Painting and Scene Finishing]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Matte Painting and Scene Finishing","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/2.5D Depth Cards and Parallax.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/2.5D Depth Cards and Parallax.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"2.5 d depth cards and parallax 2.5 d depth cards and parallax","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/2.5D Depth Cards and Parallax.md","fileName":"2.5D Depth Cards and Parallax.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"2.5D Depth Cards and Parallax","heading":"2.5D Depth Cards and Parallax","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Two-dimensional images can be placed on cards at different depths in a three-dimensional scene. A virtual camera then produces different apparent sizes and movement for the cards, including motion parallax and depth-of-field changes. This is more convincing than scaling several copies while leaving them on one flat layer, as the aircraft example in the book demonstrates. The illusion has limits: a large camera orbit can reveal that a card has no side or volume. A matte painting must choose camera motion that respects those limits.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Matte Painting and Scene Finishing","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pa